  Behaviors I'm choosing, flag them if any is wrong:
  - [1mOverwrite silently[0m, like shell [38;5;153m>[39m. A nightly rerun of the same day shouldn't need [38;5;153m--force[39m.
  - [1mParent directory must already exist[0m — we don't [38;5;153mmkdir -p[39m. Missing dir is an error, not a silently-created tree.
  - [1mA day with no billed rows is a success[0m, not an error: CSV gets a header and nothing else, JSON gets [38;5;153mtotal_cents: 0[39m
    and [38;5;153maccounts: [][39m. Cron shouldn't page anyone over a quiet day.

  [1m[38;5;153mtests/test_summarize.py[0m — TDD, tests first. Renderer tests directly, matching the existing [38;5;153mrender_text[39m test: CSV
  header plus rows, JSON round-tripped through [38;5;153mjson.loads[39m asserting [38;5;153mtotal_cents[39m and [38;5;153mday[39m, and the empty-rows case for
  both. Plus one [38;5;153mCliRunner[39m test in a new [38;5;153mtests/test_cli.py[39m that monkeypatches [38;5;153mconnect[39m/[38;5;153mdaily_rows[39m and asserts the file
  actually appears on disk with the right contents — that's the only part of this that isn't a pure function, so it's
  worth covering. The suite stays DB-free.

  [1mOut of scope / consequences[0m
  - No new dependencies; [38;5;153mcsv[39m and [38;5;153mjson[39m are stdlib. ADR-0002 is untouched — no storage change here.
  - [38;5;153mdeploy/crontab[39m doesn't change. The nightly job calls [38;5;153m/usr/local/bin/reportkit-nightly[39m, which isn't in this repo, so
    [1msomeone has to edit that wrapper by hand[0m for exports to actually happen nightly. I'd leave that to you unless you
    want the repo to carry the wrapper.
  - No version bump unless you want one — this is a feature, so a minor bump to 2.5.0 if you do.

  Does this look right? I'll wait for your go-ahead before writing any code.

